<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Woodchester opens services base in Dublin.</title>
<headline>Woodchester opens services base in Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish financial services firm Woodchester Investments said on Wednesday it was setting up a European Services Centre in Dublin to cater for the group's UK and European operations.</p>
<p>The new centre, which is being grant-aided by Irish investment agency, IDA, will create 100 new jobs providing customer care, administration and accounting services for Woodchester's clients, the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
